<title>USA: USDA's Glickman--China MFN vital to US cotton.</title>
<headline>USDA's Glickman--China MFN vital to US cotton.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>China is a leading market for U.S. cotton exports, Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman said Tuesday, in seeking cotton industry support for renewal of most favored nation trade status for Beijing.</p>
<p>Rejection of MFN would unravel U.S. trade ties and sales, Glickman said. As an example, he cited the $1 billion in U.S. cotton sold to China this marketing year.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't want to lose that,&quot; he said. &quot;We have nothing to gain and everything to lose...We need to engage China.&quot;</p>
<p>Afterward, Glickman told reporters he believed MFN would be renewed despite an unusual coalition of foes from both sides of the political spectrum.</p>
<p>&quot;My prediction is it will be approved,&quot; Glickman said, adding, &quot;It's going to have to be worked hard.&quot;</p>
</text>
